## Summary

A search tool that silently returns partial results is worse than none: an
audit that greps for callers and misses some claims a coverage it does not
have. The fff.grep issue cluster is exactly that shape: plain-mode misses,
regex classes that quietly do not match, path filters that exclude more
than asked, stale indexes serving old trees. The bar this plan sets: every
query either answers completely or says why it cannot, staleness is part
of the result, and a recall corpus runs in CI so regressions are caught
before an audit trusts them.

## Non-goals

Ranking or performance work; correctness first.

